      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction multiplies two 32-bit register values, and writes the
result to the 64-bit destination register.</p>
    <p>
        This is an alias of
        <a href="smaddl.html">SMADDL</a>.
        This means:
      </p><ul><li>
          The encodings in this description are named to match the encodings of
          <a href="smaddl.html">SMADDL</a>.
        </li><li>The description of <a href="smaddl.html">SMADDL</a> gives the operational pseudocode, any <span class="arm-defined-word">constrained unpredictable</span> behavior, and any operational information for this instruction.</li></ul>
    <p class="desc"></p><div class="regdiagram-32"><table class="regdiagram"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr">1</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="lr">1</td><td class="l">1</td><td>0</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="lr">1</td><td class="lr">0</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">1</td><td colspan="5" class="lr">Rm</td><td class="lr">0</td><td class="l">1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td class="r">1</td><td colspan="5" class="lr">Rn</td><td colspan="5" class="lr">Rd</td></tr><tr class="secondrow"><td class="droppedname">sf</td><td colspan="2" class="droppedname">op54</td><td></td><td colspan="3"></td><td></td><td class="droppedname">U</td><td colspan="2"></td><td colspan="5"></td><td class="droppedname">o0</td><td colspan="5" class="droppedname">Ra</td><td colspan="5"></td><td colspan="5"></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="encoding"><div class="encoding__label"><h4 class="encoding">Encoding</h4><a id="SMULL_SMADDL_64WA_dp_3src"></a></div><p class="asm-code">SMULL  <a href="#XdOrXZR__6" title='Is the 64-bit name of the general-purpose destination register, encoded in the "Rd" field.'>&lt;Xd&gt;</a>, <a href="#WnOrWZR__5" title='Is the 32-bit name of the first general-purpose source register holding the multiplicand, encoded in the "Rn" field.'>&lt;Wn&gt;</a>, <a href="#WmOrWZR__6" title='Is the 32-bit name of the second general-purpose source register holding the multiplier, encoded in the "Rm" field.'>&lt;Wm&gt;</a></p><p class="equivto">
      is equivalent to
    </p>
          <p class="asm-code"><a href="smaddl.html#SMADDL_64WA_dp_3src">SMADDL</a>  <a href="smaddl.html#XdOrXZR__6">&lt;Xd&gt;</a>, <a href="smaddl.html#WnOrWZR__5">&lt;Wn&gt;</a>, <a href="smaddl.html#WmOrWZR__6">&lt;Wm&gt;</a>, XZR</p>
          <p class="equivto">
          and is always the preferred disassembly.
        </p>
